<title>USA: Spring Branch, Texas, bonds not bank-qualified.</title>
<headline>Spring Branch, Texas, bonds not bank-qualified.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A $3 million Spring Branch Independent School District, Texas, deal set for competitive sale on Monday is not bank qualifed, the district's financial adviser said Friday.</p>
<p>First Southwest Co. said various information services had been incorrectly listing the issue as bank-qualified.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
